 "narr": {
  "Aqua HK": "W34 users 3,638 (-1.6% YoY) with 229 GA4 bookings (+42.2% YoY); conversion rate 6.3% vs 4.4% LY. Google delivered 80 bookings at HK$146 CPA; Meta 28 at HK$253, its strongest Meta week of the eight. Google had not fully published modelled store visits for this week when the data was pulled, so the latest point on the walk-in panel understates the true figure.",
  "Hutong HK": "W34 users 4,020 (+31.8% YoY) with 277 GA4 bookings (+7.4% YoY); conversion rate 6.9% vs 8.5% LY. Google delivered 15 bookings at HK$388 CPA; Meta 14 at HK$450. Meta spend rose to HK$6,304 because a new Mahjong reach campaign took HK$1,359 of it. That campaign buys reach and records no schedules, so it lifts the Meta cost per booking shown here without adding bookings. Google had not fully published modelled store visits for this week when the data was pulled, so the latest point on the walk-in panel understates the true figure.",
  "The Chinese Library": "W34 users 1,482 (+21.6% YoY) with 113 GA4 bookings (+46.8% YoY); conversion rate 7.6% vs 6.3% LY. Users fell 24.8% week on week from an unusually high W33. Google delivered 41 bookings at HK$72 CPA, the cheapest Google acquisition outside Dim Sum Library and Shiro; Meta 10 at HK$637. Google had not fully published modelled store visits for this week when the data was pulled, so the latest point on the walk-in panel understates the true figure.",
  "Cantina": "W34 users 1,406 (+41.7% YoY) with 79 GA4 bookings (+38.6% YoY); conversion rate 5.6% vs 5.7% LY. Google delivered 9 bookings at HK$320 CPA; Meta 11 at HK$232. Google spend has been cut by more than half since W30 and bookings have held, so the channel is running leaner. Google had not fully published modelled store visits for this week when the data was pulled, so the latest point on the walk-in panel understates the true figure.",
  "Dim Sum Library": "W34 users 986 (-0.3% YoY) with 143 GA4 bookings (+2.1% YoY); conversion rate 14.5% vs 14.2% LY. Google delivered 62 bookings at HK$21 CPA, the cheapest in the portfolio; Meta 3 at HK$377. This Google account records no walk-in conversion actions, so that panel is empty rather than zero.",
  "Shiro Pacific Place": "W34 users 670 (-10.4% YoY) with 71 GA4 bookings (-19.3% YoY); conversion rate 10.6% vs 11.8% LY. Google delivered 66 bookings at HK$61 CPA; Meta 20 at HK$263. Google had not fully published modelled store visits for this week when the data was pulled, so the latest point on the walk-in panel understates the true figure.",
  "Shiro Tai Kwun": "W34 users 1,226 with 68 GA4 bookings; conversion rate 5.5%. New in 2026, so there is no like-for-like last year. Google delivered 66 bookings at HK$61 CPA; Meta 20 at HK$263, both on the shared Shiro account. Google had not fully published modelled store visits for this week when the data was pulled, so the latest point on the walk-in panel understates the true figure.",
  "Vesu": "W34 users 1,239 (+33.8% YoY) with 73 GA4 bookings (+23.7% YoY); conversion rate 5.9% vs 6.4% LY. Google delivered 26 bookings at HK$87 CPA; Meta 15 at HK$232 from the conversion campaign, against 35 at HK$98 the week before. Vesu reopened on 8 September, so W31 is a closed week whose website figures are visits and advance bookings made before reopening, and W32 had six trading days. Google walk-in signals are not tracked in this account, so that panel is empty.",
  "The Canton Library": "The Canton Library opened on 8 September 2026, so there is no last-year line. W34 users 3,959 with 46 GA4 bookings; conversion rate 1.2%, up from 0.8%. Meta&rsquo;s conversions campaign delivered 11 bookings at HK$1,087 CPA, an improvement on HK$1,559 the week before; the awareness campaign (HK$2,990 this week) optimises to landing page views and carries no cost per booking. Google spent HK$13,916 this week but has no booking conversion recording, so Google bookings and CPA are not available rather than zero. W31 was a pre-opening week, shown as a gap."
 },
